<h1>.agents/ Index</h1>
<p>Deep reference for <code>&lt;project-name&gt;</code>. The root <code>AGENTS.md</code> states each rule in one line and links here for the detail; this file is the table of contents an agent reads before opening any of them.</p>
<p>One row per file. The <code>Contents</code> cell says what a reader finds there and when it is worth the tokens, in one sentence. A file that earns no row has no reason to exist here.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&lt;topic-1&gt;.md (&lt;topic-1&gt;.md)</td><td>&lt;What it covers, the rules it carries, and the evidence behind them&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>&lt;topic-2&gt;.md (&lt;topic-2&gt;.md)</td><td>&lt;What it covers and the one decision it records&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>&lt;topic-3&gt;.md (&lt;topic-3&gt;.md)</td><td>&lt;What it covers; name the gotcha it exists to prevent&gt;</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Related, outside <code>.agents/</code>:</p>
<ul><li><code>docs/&lt;spec&gt;.md</code> — &lt;the spec this directory's files elaborate on&gt;</li><li><code>.aidocs/conventions/</code> — &lt;corpus or repo conventions that apply here&gt;</li></ul>
<p>Rules this index follows (from the docs convention):</p>
<ul><li>Every file under <code>.agents/</code> appears exactly once in the table above.</li><li>The root <code>AGENTS.md</code> stays within its 20-80 line budget; anything past that moves here and</li></ul>
<p>gets a row.</p>
<ul><li>A row is a sentence, not a paragraph. Detail lives in the file the row points at.</li><li>Paths are relative to this directory; no absolute paths, no links into another repo.</li></ul>
